<% content_for :title, "Media Query" %>
<div class="mb-8">
  <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Utilities</p>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">Media Query</h1>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground">
    A <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">matchMedia</code> watcher.
    Writes <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">data-media-matches</code>
    on its element, toggles an optional class, and dispatches
    <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">ui--media-query:change</code>.
    Sidebar and Drawer read it for responsive layout; it renders nothing itself.
  </p>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Preview</h2>
<div id="media-query-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted p-8 mb-8">
  <div data-controller="ui--media-query"
       data-ui--media-query-query-value="(min-width: 768px)"
       data-ui--media-query-matches-class="border-primary bg-primary/5"
       class="rounded-lg border-2 border-border p-8 text-center transition-colors">
    <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
      Resize the window across <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">768px</code>.
      The border and fill switch when the query matches -- open devtools to watch
      <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">data-media-matches</code> flip on this element.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground">Query: <code>(min-width: 768px)</code></p>
  </div>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Usage</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800 mb-8">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-neutral-900 px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-neutral-400">ERB</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#media-query-usage" class="text-xs text-neutral-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-neutral-950 px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed" tabindex="0"><code id="media-query-usage" class="text-neutral-200"><%= h(example_media_query_usage) %></code></pre>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Options</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-muted">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Name</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Type</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
      <% [
        ["query (value)",   "String", "The media query to watch, e.g. \"(min-width: 768px)\"."],
        ["matches (class)", "String", "Optional. Toggled on the element while the query matches."],
        ["data-media-matches", "attribute", "Always written, \"true\" or \"false\", from connect() onward."],
        ["ui--media-query:change", "event", "Dispatched on every change, with { matches, query } in event.detail."],
      ].each do |name, type, desc| %>
        <tr class="hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary"><%= name %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= type %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= desc %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Notes</h2>
<ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 list-disc list-inside">
  <li>Removes its <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">change</code> listener on <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">disconnect()</code> -- an element that leaves the DOM leaves nothing subscribed behind.</li>
  <li>Geometry and visibility are not this primitive's job -- it only ever reports breakpoint state.</li>
</ul>
